# Iluminate UI And Persistence Context

This project must follow the presentation and navigation standard already proven in
`/srv/voxalia/services/web/voxalia`. Do not invent one-off workbench screens when a
Voxalia pattern exists.

## Source Standard Reviewed

Reference modules:

- Voxalia Asterisk Tenant Profiles list:
  `/srv/voxalia/services/web/voxalia/components/crud/asterisk-profiles-crud.tsx`
- Voxalia Asterisk tenant workspace:
  `/srv/voxalia/services/web/voxalia/components/workspace/asterisk-workspace.tsx`
  and `/srv/voxalia/services/web/voxalia/components/workspace/workspace-page.tsx`
- Voxalia Asterisk Infrastructure workspace:
  `/srv/voxalia/services/web/voxalia/components/workspace/asterisk-infrastructure-placeholder.tsx`
- Shared CRUD primitives:
  `/srv/voxalia/services/web/voxalia/components/crud/crud-resource-page.tsx`
  and `/srv/voxalia/services/web/voxalia/components/crud/crud-grid.tsx`

## Navigation Pattern

Top-level menu items open list or workspace pages through stable routes.

List route pattern:

- Page shell uses `AppShell` with `currentPath` set to the menu route.
- Page header appears above the grid:
  - badges for status/context/role when available;
  - `h1` page title;
  - short description;
  - optional `FeedbackAlert`.
- Main content is a `CrudResourcePage`, not a custom card list.

Detail route pattern:

- Opening a row goes to a stable detail route, for example:
  `/settings/asterisk/[tenantKey]`.
- Detail keeps the sidebar menu selected by passing the parent `currentPath`.
- Detail renders a workspace component.
- Workspace contains:
  - top header with context badges, title, description and back link;
  - optional summary metrics;
  - a tab bar in a bordered `bg-card` strip;
  - one active tab body at a time.

Do not rely on query parameters as the main identity route for editable resources
when the resource has its own workspace. Query parameters are acceptable for tab
selection and scoped filters.

## Grid Pattern

Resource collections are shown with `CrudResourcePage` plus `CrudGrid`.

Grid standard:

- Toolbar card above the table.
- Search input on the left with `Search` icon.
- Select filters next to search.
- `Clear` button with `Filter` icon.
- Create button on the right when `canCreate !== false`.
- Main grid inside a `Card`.
- Card header shows:
  - title;
  - description;
  - badges for shown and total counts.
- Table header is always visible and explicit.
- Table rows use stable height, border separators, hover background.
- Numeric columns are right-aligned and usually monospace.
- Status fields render with `Badge`.
- First identifying column usually shows a primary label plus a secondary key.

Avoid unlabeled form-like rows pretending to be a grid. If it is tabular, it must
have table/grid headers.

## Row Actions Pattern

Voxalia uses two kinds of row actions:

- Built-in CRUD actions from `allowedActions`:
  - `view`: icon-only `Eye`;
  - `edit`: icon-only `Pencil`;
  - `delete` / `deactivate`: icon-only `Trash2`;
  - `workspace`: icon-only `ArrowUpRight`.
- Custom `_actions`:
  - rendered as compact text button plus `ArrowUpRight`;
  - used for explicit row navigation/action labels.

Actions live in a right-aligned `Actions` column.

Do not invent per-page action styling. If Iluminate needs custom labels such as
`Open`, `Duplicate`, or `Simulate`, they must be handled deliberately and
consistently with this action model.

## Workspace Pattern

Workspaces are for editing or operating inside one selected parent resource.

Workspace standard:

- Header and back link at the top.
- Tabs in a dedicated bordered `bg-card` container.
- Tabs should map to business sections, not visual whims.
- Tab bodies may contain:
  - overview cards;
  - `CrudResourcePage` grids with `hideToolbar` / `hideHeader` where nested;
  - explicit records tables for read-only operational data;
  - master-detail grids for child entities.
- Nested sections still use search, filters, grid headers and row actions.
- Modals use shared `CrudFormDialog` or `Modal`.
- Empty states use `EmptyState`.

## Iluminate Partitura Application

The current Partitura Generator must be realigned to this standard.

Correct high-level flow:

1. `Partituras` menu opens a list grid of partituras for the active client.
2. A row action opens a partitura workspace route.
3. The partitura workspace contains tabs, for example:
   - `Overview`: project/partitura summary and validation status.
   - `Scenes`: scenes grid; selected scene can expose clips grid.
   - `Layout`: chains, segments and zones as explicit grids.
   - `Simulator`: output preview, Generate, Play/Pause, Reset, timing metrics.
   - `Export`: generated JSON only when it becomes operationally useful.
4. Scenes, clips, segments and zones must not be edited as arbitrary stacked
   cards if they are collections. They should be grids or master-detail grids.
5. Cards are acceptable for summaries, selected-record detail panels, metrics and
   simulator preview, but not as a replacement for CRUD grids.

## Partitura Domain Rule

Iluminate does not model partitura revisions.

- One project has one current persisted partitura.
- Generated JSON must not include `revision`.
- Persistence must not use a partitura revisions table as the business model.
- If a user wants a variant, they duplicate the partitura into a separate
  partitura/project record and edit that record.
- `schemaVersion` is only a wire-format compatibility marker for core/firmware.

## Persistence Implication

Continuing with in-memory partitura state will cause UI rework later. Before
building more simulator/editor surface, introduce a stable persistence model:

- `iluminate.projects`: client-scoped installation/project.
- `iluminate.partituras`: one editable current partitura per project.
- Child configuration may be persisted either as normalized child tables or as a
  JSON document while the editor model stabilizes, but the API contract must
  expose resources in the same shape used by the workspace grids.

The web should stop treating the Partitura Generator as a temporary local-only
workbench. It should become the partitura workspace backed by API/storage.

## Implementation Mandate

Before changing Iluminate UI:

1. Check this `.context`.
2. Prefer copying/adapting Voxalia primitives over inventing new layout.
3. Keep list pages as `CrudResourcePage`.
4. Keep detail pages as workspace pages with tabs.
5. Use grids for resource collections.
6. Use shared CRUD dialogs/actions.
7. Add persistence when the screen edits business resources that must survive
   navigation or later deployment.

